What does an orphaned tx look like via rpc?
<p>I am testing with a currency forked from Pivx, but I see that bitcoind responds the same way here <a href="https://bitcointalk.org/index.php?topic=100824.0" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://bitcointalk.org/index.php?topic=100824.0</a> with error code -5</p>
<p><strong>If I send/receive a tx that then some time after a few confirmations (the block) was to become orphaned or stale; Would I get the same reply from rpc gettransactions as below (where I intentionally typed a non transaction id in) if I were to look for the tx or should it come back with a full tx object?</strong></p>
<pre><code>zdx-cli gettransaction &quot;gyyyyf&quot;
error: {&quot;code&quot;:-5,&quot;message&quot;:&quot;Invalid or non-wallet transaction id&quot;}
</code></pre>
